+## Session failure handling
+
+- `beforeSession` is inside the `try` block, so a throw there reaches the `catch`/`finally` blocks, firing both `onError` and `afterSession`, where a deployer can assume no tools were run and the turn was aborted before provider interaction ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+
+## Failed session startup
+
+- `afterSession` runs even if `beforeSession` allocated a resource and then failed; cleanup must tolerate partial allocation and cannot assume that startup completed ([validated by: releases a partially allocated resource when beforeSession rejects](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.failedStart.test.ts#L8)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
